---

## PERMISSIONS

These are still wrong and I think we need to be clear about which permissions are needed to do what and where things are currently unclear and wrong.

Let us assume we have issue `#a` in `a/a` and issue `#b` in `b/b`. 

I'm going to say `#a <- #b` for `#a` depends on `#b` or `#b` blocks `#a` or `#a` is blocked by `#b`

Now we need to consider the following actions:

### `CreateIssueDependency` `POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{index}/dependencies` & `CreateIssueBlocking`  `POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{index}/blocks`

This is (for appropriate `#a` & `#b`):

```
SET #a <- #b
```

To set `#a` depends on/blocked by `#b` (`#a <- #b`), we need the following permissions:
    * `a/a` has to have dependencies enabled
    * We need to write to `#a`, i.e. Write to issues/pulls in `a/a`
    * if `a/a` & `b/b` are not the same repo we need to allow cross repo dependencies
    * We need to be able to see `b/b` i.e. `b/b` is accessible 
    * We need to be able to read `#b` i.e. Read issues/pull in `b/b`

There are two endpoints that do this in your PR - I have tried to make it clearer which way round things are.

* `POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{index}/dependencies`
  * Let us define `<issue>` as the issue referred to by `{index}`
  * and `<formIssue>` as the issue referred to by the body form.
  * This makes `<issue>` depend on `<formIssue>`, i.e. `<issue>` is blocked by `<formIssue>`
  * I.E. `SET <issue> <- <formIssue>`
* `POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{index}/blocks`
  * I.e. `SET <formIssue> <- <issue>`

The PR as it stands does not do this correctly and the code is confusing especially with the passing of the dependencyblock type.

